# 7. Tool Specification

---

## investigate_order

### Purpose

Investigates an order across multiple operational systems and identifies the most probable root cause preventing fulfillment.

### Input

```json
{
  "orderId": "ORD-102"
}
```

### Internal Workflow

```text
Validate Order

↓

Load Order

↓

Load Payment

↓

Load Inventory

↓

Load Shipment

↓

Apply Business Rules

↓

Determine Root Cause

↓

Generate Recommendation
```

### Output

```json
{
  "status": "BLOCKED",
  "rootCause": "Payment Failed",
  "confidence": 0.96,
  "evidence": [
    "Payment authorization failed",
    "Inventory available",
    "Shipment not created"
  ],
  "recommendedAction": "retry_payment"
}
```

### Failure Cases

- Order not found
- Invalid Order ID
- Missing commerce records

---

## execute_resolution

### Purpose

Safely performs predefined operational actions.

### Supported Actions

- retry_payment
- release_inventory
- recreate_shipment

### Input

```json
{
  "orderId": "ORD-102",
  "action": "retry_payment"
}
```

### Output

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Payment retried successfully.",
  "updatedStatus": "READY_FOR_FULFILLMENT"
}
```

### Validation

Only predefined actions may be executed.

Arbitrary operations are rejected.

---

## get_order_timeline

### Purpose

Returns the chronological operational history of an order.

### Input

```json
{
  "orderId": "ORD-102"
}
```

### Output

```json
{
  "timeline": [
    "Order Created",
    "Payment Failed",
    "Inventory Reserved",
    "Shipment Pending"
  ]
}
```

---

## find_orders_needing_attention

### Purpose

Returns orders requiring immediate operational review.

### Example Criteria

- Failed payment
- Inventory unavailable
- Shipment delayed
- Missing fulfillment

### Output

```json
[
  {
    "orderId": "ORD-102",
    "priority": "HIGH",
    "reason": "Payment Failed"
  }
]
```

